-- and from the configured molecule, computed: eight. One splitting, at the gamma methylene. The record
-- shows it: the standard random-coil table gives isoleucine's gamma methylene as two resonances, 1.48
-- and 1.19 ppm, against one value for each of the other groups (gamma methyl 0.95, delta methyl 0.89,
-- beta 1.90, alpha 4.23, amide 8.19). Isoleucine is the case where the field's own table carries the
-- split outright, because 1.48 and 1.19 are far apart; valine's 0.97 and 0.94 and leucine's 0.94 and
-- 0.90 are the hard ones, and leucine's beta methylene is reported as a single value. The size of the
-- splitting is a fact about the molecule's geometry; whether the instrument resolves it is not.
il-signals-conf : class-count Ile il-eq il-rank il-conf-gens 22 il-h ≡ 8
il-signals-conf = λ i → 8
